ritance, including persistence and correct behavior after a confirmed node reboot.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots do not inspect /srv/releases or the release-team group, so those final details rely on the captured executor commands.","The restart protocol clearly shows acknowledgement, an actual boot-ID change corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovery of the filesystem, data, workspace metadata, and inheritance behavior. However, node1 was systemd-degraded both before and after the reboot because of a pre-existing failed ssh.service, so the evidence does not demonstrate a fully healthy whole-node service baseline and recovery (cmd-6cad4c85ec5b4215, global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services, global:after_executor:node1:failed-services)."]}
